###### 5.2.1. Project Activities Standards 

In the search for best practices, the mining companies search specialist companies in their respective areas of performance.  Thus, it is common that in only one project there are several companies involved in the development of the feasibility studies. The problems, in the majority, are: 

- The existence of several Cost Estimate Criteria; 

- Several Material Take-offs with different Technical Descriptions; 

- Activities that disrespect the local supplying market; 

