These problems have the following consequences: 

- Equal Activities with different unit prices; 

- One activity in a engineering company that corresponds to two or more activities in another engineering companies; 

- Activities with different names but with the same technical description and unit price; 

- Unit prices higher than local market in function of services specifications not normally executed; 

Thus, it is very important that the engineering companies develop the Material Take-offs using the Technical Descriptions and the Standard Quantities Spreadsheet of the Project, guaranteeing its constructability (respecting the local market) and not in its own local standards, beyond the estimate being elaborated following the criteria established in the Work Breakdown Structure of the Project for the later stage of loading resources with the activities Planning. 

